{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that ship as separate library targets (","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","level":3,"text":"Importing at call sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but that re-exports ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice (","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action (","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" file:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The easy case to forget is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that reads the slice for display — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"text":"Comparison","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Comparison"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"text":"The Decision Rule","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"text":"Hook Selection Guide","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Registration Order","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next Steps","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","role":"symbol","title":"PluginHost","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/P